  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Fe</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CO</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>4</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo></msup></math></p><p>Oxidation no. of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>26</mn></msub><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>Ar</mi><mn>18</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CO</mi></math> is a Strong field ligand, so paring occurs against the Hund&#39;s rule.&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>eg</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Number of unpaired electron <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;</p><p>so magnetic moment <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></math> B.M.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</m